// Equivalently, we need to find a connected subgraph of size k (which will be the first k nodes in some DFS preorder) 
// where all nodes have a[i] >= X, and this subgraph can be the first k nodes of a DFS preorder starting from some root.

// Actually, the first k nodes in a DFS preorder form a connected set. Moreover, for any connected set S of size k, 
