// Then we need to order the neighbors so that DFS visits all nodes in S before visiting any node outside S.
// This is possible if and only if for every node v in S, the number of neighbors of v that are in S is at least 1 (for non-root) 
// or we can control the order. Actually, we just need that the DFS doesn't leave S before visiting all k nodes.
// This is possible if and only if S is connected (which it is) and we can order the neighbors appropriately.
